# Impactful decisions must be captured as Cursor rules

Whenever we make an impactful decision in this repository, we must capture it as a **new Cursor rule** (`.mdc`) under `.cursor/rules/decisions/` **in the same change/PR**.

## What counts as “impactful”

Create a decision record for any change that materially affects one or more of:

- Architecture or design direction
- Data model, storage format, migrations, or persistence choices
- Dependency additions/removals or major upgrades (including tooling)
- Public interfaces (APIs, CLIs, exported libraries), file formats, or breaking behavior changes
- Security/privacy posture, authn/authz, secrets handling
- Performance/scalability trade-offs or caching strategy
- Testing strategy or CI behavior that changes how we validate correctness
- Operational workflows (deployment, release, backup/restore, environment configuration)

If unsure, treat it as impactful and write the decision record.

## How to write it

- Create a new rule file at `.cursor/rules/decisions/YYYY-MM-DD-short-title.mdc`.
- Start from `.cursor/rules/decisions/0000-template.mdc`.
- Set applicability based on the type/scope of the change:
  - Repo-wide decision → `alwaysApply: true` (no `globs`)
  - Area-specific decision → `globs: path/**`
  - Language/tool-specific decision → `globs: **/*.{ext1,ext2}` (or the closest matching patterns)
- Keep it short and specific:
  - Context + decision
  - Constraints we must not violate
  - Consequences/trade-offs
  - When/why this decision might be revisited

## Workflow requirement

Before implementing an impactful change, explicitly state (in chat and/or PR description) that you will:

- Create the decision rule first (or in the same commit)
- Link the decision rule path in the PR description (or commit message)

Do not proceed with impactful changes without capturing the decision record.
